{
  "case_id": "2020-20-222",
  "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:00 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Goldman Sachs Group, Inc. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In this case, the court of appeals upheld the certification of a securities class action based on exceptionally generic and aspirational statements in the face of overwhelming and unrebutted evidence that the statements had no impact on the stock price."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shanmugam",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the more generic a statement, the less likely it is that it will contain the type of information that is incorporated into the market price of the stock. And we think that in this case, the statements are exceedingly generic, and, where that is true, that is powerful or compelling evidence."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So can I just stop you there? If we conclude that it's generic but not exceedingly generic, you're drawing a distinction between those two things, is that not powerful evidence?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shanmugam",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that is correct. And the Second Circuit, I think, failed to navigate between Amgen and Halliburton II and its dictates that all relevant evidence should be considered."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sopan Joshi",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0001-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The dispute on the first question presented has narrowed substantially. Petitioners no longer maintain that a generic statement categorically precludes a finding of price impact. It doesn't."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Do you think it's the best reading of what it did?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Okay. So the presumption isn't irrebuttable or irrefutable. It is rebuttable somehow?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0002-0002",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the more generic a statement, the less likely it actually had a price impact in the particular case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Well, you just told us\nwe should say don't reintroduce the materiality\nissue. Do you mean to say that we should\nprovide the following instruction: In\nconsidering whether the Basic presumption has\nbeen rebutted, you may not consider any evidence\nthat would also go to the issue of materiality?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: The credible\nevidence of no direct impact against a theory.\nWhat's a district judge supposed to do?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 81,
        "start": 81
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: And on the how we\ngot here question that you start -- started with, I think\nwe're here in part maybe because of confusion in some of the lower courts about\nhow to read Amgen and Halliburton II together."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: Do you think it would be an insult?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: So vacating it would be okay with you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-20-222",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b6d95fd705c30e3e4949478a941ad1732bc3e16371c034b458d3b6e7abdf4ee7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b6d95fd705c3-0004-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 92,
        "start": 92
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
